{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-17357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+{50}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\\,x={b}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-17357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+{50}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 5x+{50}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={265}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={53}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=53.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-17357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87ea9cfa4ccce17c50f1a89e1a1a15a3e248f5b7f7e95e772b9d614dde9e1d63"} {"question" "q-17357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-17357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "53"] ["math" "55"] ["math" "63"] ["math" "73"] ["math" "75"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-17357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "53"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-42790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12})=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+6\\pi n,\\,x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+6\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-42790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\,\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}=-\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi , & \\,\\frac{x}{3}=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x=-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+6n\\pi , & \\,x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+6n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-42790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87ea9cfa4ccce17c50f1a89e1a1a15a3e248f5b7f7e95e772b9d614dde9e1d63"} {"question" "q-42790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-42790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5\\pi }{9}"] ["math" "-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-42790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\cdot {30}^{∘}+2\\cdot n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={60}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87ea9cfa4ccce17c50f1a89e1a1a15a3e248f5b7f7e95e772b9d614dde9e1d63"} {"question" "q-121063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "120"] ["math" "150"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "60"] ["math" "90"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{18}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{18}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87ea9cfa4ccce17c50f1a89e1a1a15a3e248f5b7f7e95e772b9d614dde9e1d63"} {"question" "q-121066" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121066" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{18}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{9}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{9}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{18}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121066" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{18}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx={180}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘},\\,x={a}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,\\frac{x}{3}={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx={180}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘},\\,x={360}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=360.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87ea9cfa4ccce17c50f1a89e1a1a15a3e248f5b7f7e95e772b9d614dde9e1d63"} {"question" "q-121071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "240"] ["math" "270"] ["math" "360"] ["math" "450"] ["math" "480"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"} {"question" "q-121071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "360"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012449/state.json" "file_sha256" "ada9f67ea6f8dd0cd37ba18c5e745770ca9cf3e7d4f8d87d9784a79e94c64a9b"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1160 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
